OASIS Standard, 6 October 2025. Open Document Format for Office Applications
(OpenDocument) Version 1.4, Part 4: Recalculated Formula (OpenFormula) Format.
Source: https://docs.oasis-open.org/office/OpenDocument/v1.4/os/part4-formula/

Redistributed verbatim. The OASIS terms forbid modifying the document itself,
including by adding to or removing its notices - which is why this sidecar file
exists instead of an SPDX header inside the .html.

Verifying this copy: it will NOT hash-match a fresh download, and that is expected.
The OASIS site sits behind Cloudflare, whose email-obfuscation rewrites the authors'
mailto: addresses into __cf_email__ / data-cfemail attributes using a key that
rotates per request. Byte length is unchanged (1845912) and the differences are
confined to those attributes; the specification text is identical. To check, diff a
fresh fetch and confirm every hunk is a __cf_email__ span:

  curl -sSL -o /tmp/p4.html \
    https://docs.oasis-open.org/office/OpenDocument/v1.4/os/part4-formula/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part4-formula.html
  diff /tmp/p4.html doc/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part4-formula.html | grep -v cf_email

The PDF at the same stage is not rewritten and hashes stably, if an archival copy
that can be verified by hash alone is ever wanted.
